{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"9f45831a9dcddaff012f0bffc3c4cacecf4cc1a72469fc5513e9f45d911c1e88","slug":"modeling.posterior-predictive-checks","location":"/modeling/posterior_predictive_checks.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Posterior Predictive Checks","content_includes_title":false,"keywords":["Uncertainty","Quantification","Reinforcement Learning","Bayesian Inference","Active Inference"],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"posterior_predictive_checks.md","url":"/tambi-website//build/posterior_predictive-b960b10c220a2d2b0e39d4917f0b1b43.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This section documents the posterior predictive checks (PPCs) that drove the\ndevelopment of the inference agent from its five-parameter form to the final\nsix-parameter version. I’d like to guide you through why a misspecification was\nsuspected, how it was diagnosed, what change resolved it, and exactly how well\nthe final model reproduces participant behaviour, including the residual\ndiscrepancies that remain by design. All checks are reproducible via\n","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"PBfR877NNS"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posterior_predictive_checks.py","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"KTdrxPfvkX"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"LJoqIrNK0u"}],"key":"e84wqa9S5Q"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rationale","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"eft4vIGOCi"}],"identifier":"rationale","label":"Rationale","html_id":"rationale","implicit":true,"key":"jwoirTZFyB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameter recovery and simulation-based calibration establish that the inference network ","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"UCahfvPDqK"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"inverts the agent correctly","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"xH8nxJBj7E"}],"key":"C7b4x7RLcK"},{"type":"text","value":". They do not establish that the ","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"PsvwcABotu"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"agent","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"X57HTs1jRQ"}],"key":"pKVoWyXf79"},{"type":"text","value":" reproduces real behaviour. A posterior predictive check closes this gap: for each participant we draw parameter sets from the posterior, simulate the agent on that participant’s exact trial schedule, extract the same behavioural features from the simulated and the observed data, and ask whether the observed feature value falls within the simulated posterior-predictive interval. A feature whose observed value lies ","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"gjGOqa3TMn"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"above","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"GT17yslsH4"}],"key":"DfFpO10iGV"},{"type":"text","value":" the 95% predictive interval signals that the agent cannot produce enough of that behaviour - a misspecification.","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"wqYyNI8b2N"}],"key":"UU8KtrYfIZ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The checks focus on a panel of “switchiness” features that capture how sharply\nand how often participants change their net placement, since this turned out to be the most critical part. Specificially, the features are the spontaneous switch rate, the fraction of large trial-to-trial shifts, the mean trial shift, belief lability, the oddball-following measures, and the within-state placement variability. These are the behaviours most diagnostic of the inference-level and action-level parameters.","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"Mkz0MZTXKH"}],"key":"fVhdwV0r4t"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The five-parameter misspecification","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"QwoxzUkRzh"}],"identifier":"the-five-parameter-misspecification","label":"The five-parameter misspecification","html_id":"the-five-parameter-misspecification","implicit":true,"key":"gXSKPnO14z"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the five-parameter agent (deterministic belief-to-action mapping), the PPCs revealed a systematic and pervasive failure, namely that across participants, essentially ","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"FIOOPQMYXb"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"every","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"L5Xp4mZlyw"}],"key":"mEOeJ3o3xF"},{"type":"text","value":" switchiness feature fell above the 95% predictive interval. The agent was uniformly ","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"Ygn3peslHc"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"too stable","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"K4JHFUKU4D"}],"key":"Pj7H4OmL4x"},{"type":"text","value":" - it could not reproduce the trial-to-trial variability participants actually show. A representative diagnosis traced a systematic bias of approximately 27° in switchy/oddball-shift features.","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"WtTFM9c7I4"}],"key":"za6RKqmv70"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Crucially, this was not a failure of the inference step (recovery and SBC were clean) but of the generative model: with a deterministic mapping from belief to action, the agent placed its nets at exactly the predictive mean on every trial, whereas participants still scatter their placements around it over trials.","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"w1zF0sFyVo"}],"key":"Pbqar41yEz"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Diagnostic chain","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"SaXkIv63rs"}],"identifier":"diagnostic-chain","label":"Diagnostic chain","html_id":"diagnostic-chain","implicit":true,"key":"cdflpICpuf"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before adding any parameter, the source of the excess variability was localised through a structured set of diagnostics, ruling out alternatives in turn:","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"kBR4uroHqJ"}],"key":"i9t7EUkFEL"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,